{
 "about": [
  "Astvaldr's keymap and its layer lighting: every layer, keyed by switch name (switches.json). This file is the only source; gen_astvaldr.py turns it into the firmware. Every layer names every switch: there is no fall-through, and KC_NO is a key that does nothing.",
  "Keycodes are QMK's (C(...), LGUI(LALT(...)) and so on are a whole shortcut on one key). A name from 'cursor_follow' is a key that taps its shortcut, waits the generator's CURSOR_FOLLOW_DELAY_MS, then taps 'then' (KDE's Move Mouse to Focus), so the pointer follows the window.",
  "Lighting: 'colors' names a hue and saturation each (QMK's 0-255 scale; 'off' is dark). A layer's optional 'lighting' has 'effect' (an effect, by its QMK name, that runs while the layer is on, without being saved; leaving the layer puts the saved effect back) and 'paint' (drawn on top of the running effect, at the current brightness, while it is the highest layer that is on). Each paint entry is a color and 'keys': a list of switches, or 'working' (every key on the layer that is not KC_NO) or 'dead' (every KC_NO key)."
 ],
 "cursor_follow": {
  "then": "LGUI(KC_F5)",
  "keys": {
